    {
      "repo": "zzh20188/GKI_KernelSU_SUSFS",
      "sha": "95a5710108ff16941ddecc50264737b13b0e5d07",
      "tree": "1bc09e6d09215a4bda72f8cce1e5aa83f5e06104",
      "date": "2026-11-06T19:06:23Z",
      "message": "fix: add missing KSU_SUSFS_PRIORITY_UID_FILTER Kconfig for SukiSU builtin\n\nUpstream susfs4ksu (2026-11-02, \"Make priority_uid_filter as new feature\")\nguards the declarations and definitions of susfs_set_priority_uid_filter()\nand susfs_parse_priority_app_strings() behind CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_PRIORITY_UID_FILTER,\nwhich is introduced by 10_enable_susfs_for_ksu.patch. SukiSU builtin does not\napply that patch and its Kconfig lacks the option, yet it calls both helpers\nunconditionally, so every SukiSU SUSFS build fails with implicit declarations.\n\nAppend the upstream Kconfig entry when the KSU source uses these helpers and\nthe option is missing, and enable it in the SUSFS defconfig fragment."
    }
